`cpanfile` writes most requirements as

    requires 'Carp'                         => '0';
    requires 'JSON::MaybeXS'                => '0';
    requires 'LWP::UserAgent'               => '0';

The sibling distributions of the fleet (p5-www-mikrotik, p5-www-dnsmadeeasy, p5-www-vastai) write the same block without a version:

    requires 'Carp';
    requires 'JSON::MaybeXS';

`=> '0'` means "any version" and only adds noise; the house style names the prerequisites by name.

Done when: the cpanfile uses the same block as the sibling distributions (no version on the runtime requirements), sorted alphabetically, and the test suite stays green. No behaviour change, so no red proof needed - but the file must not change the set of prerequisites.


